<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST-Dutch April CPI seen rising 2.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Dutch April CPI seen rising 2.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists forecast Dutch April consumer price inflation to show a two percent rise on an annual basis, unchanged from March.</p>
<p>Rabo and Nib Securities said lower oil prices were likely to have affected consumer prices in April. Rabo also pointed out fresh fruit and vegetable prices were lower.</p>
<p>The April cpi data are due to be published at 0830 GMT on Tuesday of next week.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date--Period--Indicator------Consensus---Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0830 13/5  April   CPI Yr/Yr	 2.0 pct    1.8/2.2    2.0</p>
<p> 0830 13/5  April   CPI Mth/Mth     0.1 pct    nil/0.4    0.6</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, NIB Securities, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
